**Changes**
- `src/store.js` — added `clearCompleted(store)`: filters out done tasks and returns how many were removed; exported it. Also fixed a pre-existing bug in `countDone` — it filtered on `t.title` instead of `t.done`, so it counted every non-empty task as done. This mattered because the count line (`tasks.length - countDone`) would have shown "0 tasks left" after clearing.
- `index.html` — added a `<button id="clear">Clear completed</button>` below the task list.
- `src/app.js` — imported `clearCompleted` and wired the button to it, followed by a re-render.
- `test/run.js` — new `clearCompleted` test: three tasks, two toggled done, asserts it returns 2 and only the open task remains.

**Verified:** `npm test` → 5 passed, including the new test. The browser wiring (button click → render) is not covered by the test suite, which only tests the store module.
